  "methodology": [
    "Production ViewCache, codecs, storage worker and OPFS; actual Go HTTP endpoints. No mocked data or Node server.",
    "Cold means an empty client replica, not cold server RAM or filesystem caches. Each workload has its own namespace; warm passes reuse normal application caches.",
    "Timings end at data-ready delivery. First-page delivery is measured separately. DOM painting and layout are not included.",
    "Three independent browser profiles per variant, run sequentially. Setup/bootstrap is recorded separately in raw results.",
    "Canonical ingress bytes hash identically across all three server builds. Explicit INFO and status-503 filters avoid differing default diagnostic scope.",
    "Historical matching runs on the server. Current Tantivy retains that path for library-strategy comparison. Current local matching replicates the complete selected window and runs in the client; its work is substantially larger.",
    "Command durations include worker queueing and overlap; do not sum them as CPU time.",
    "The screenshot's particular Safari cache was not replayed. These measurements do not prove its exact 21-second latency is eliminated."
  ],
