  "findings": [
    "The prior collector already supported arbitrary time ranges, bounded 4 MiB/4096-record transfers, coalesced reads and publication after data writes.",
    "The new planner split long ranges by day, reopening collection sessions and republishing metadata. Keep early-hour/day page delivery, then stream the remaining range through the existing collector.",
    "The new local path bypassed the existing 32 MiB event cache. It now reuses that cache after identity and completion checks, with reset and retention invalidation.",
    "Batch time-receipt queries; reuse unchanged discovery receipts instead of repeating the same metadata read.",
    "Reuse bounded decoded immutable metadata revisions while rereading the commit root under each lease.",
    "Broad cold client searches remain slower than server-selected pages. The 30-day client workload transfers 15.72 MB, versus 0.24\u20130.26 MB for the server-selected page.",
    "The local timing groups are currently coarse instrumentation, not a mandatory planner pipeline. Fine-grained action, preparation and rendering spans remain unmeasured."
  ]
